  "answer": "Mode in the view lists CSS, HTML, JavaScript, Markdown, Plain Text. Picking CSS turns the view's Display Source Code on at once, the panel's and the block wait. Markdown or HTML leave the switch as it was. On Close the block takes the mode and the switch, both ways: switch on shows the pre, switch off in the view and Close renders the HTML again, and the panel follows. So yes, it reaches the block on closing. It also gives rows up: 3 lines of HTML in 6 rows become the source in 3 rows. The old note said a change adds rows but never gives them up: that's wrong.",
